# keypunch: types onto an 80-column card (holes punched a column a key); a tab moves to the next tab stop, Return feeds a new card,
# Backspace steps back a column, Control-D ends the program by itself. Letters are typed in lower case: the program shows them as capitals,
# and a shifted letter is the keypunch's digit shift (shift turns UIOJKLM<> into 123456789). The pointer stands inside the window so the keys reach it.
move 300 100
type hello icon
key Tab
type 1966
wait
key Return
type ab
key BackSpace
type c
wait
keydown Control_L
key d
keyup Control_L
